      <h2>About ZIFF Festival Center</h2>
      <div>Zanzibar International Film Festival (ZIFF) Center in Stone Town is the permanent home of East Africa's longest-running cultural festival, celebrating African cinema, music, and arts since 1997. Year-round, the center hosts film screenings, workshops, art exhibitions, and cultural events celebrating Swahili coast heritage and African diaspora creativity. The annual July festival attracts filmmakers, artists, and audiences from across Africa and beyond. The center's courtyard and screening rooms provide a vibrant cultural hub in the heart of Stone Town.</div>
